For ASCII P3: `while(true)` reading numbers — each iteration needs 3 numbers; at EOF read fails → break. Memory = file-proportional. Then size check fails → false.

So where's the actual bug described? "uses potentially infinite loops" — in newer code maybe the loop `while (!streamer.at_end())`? But this 2022 version: hmm.

Wait — `read_comment`: `while (streamer.read(byte))` bounded by EOF. `read_whitespace`: bounded. All loops consume a byte each iteration → bounded by data size. Except... look very carefully at `read_number`:

